## Level-Triggered Epoll Behavior

With level-triggered mode, epoll will:
1. Only notify you when the socket is ready for writing
2. Continue to notify until all data is written

This means we shouldn't get EAGAIN/EWOULDBLOCK errors if we're only writing when epoll says the socket is writable, eliminating the need to check errno.

