## Important Notes

1. After removing a listener socket, the server won't be able to accept new connections on that endpoint until you recreate the socket

2. If the socket is critical (e.g., your main port 80 listener), you might want to implement a `recreate_listener` method that:
   - Finds which VirtualServer was assigned to this listener
   - Creates a new socket for the same host:port
   - Registers it with epoll
   - Updates your maps/vectors

3. In most production servers, listener socket errors are rare and usually indicate serious system issues that may require manual intervention

This implementation ensures clean removal of the listener socket and prevents resource leaks.

