    **`SA_RESTART` Flag:**
    When installing a signal handler with `sigaction()`, you can use the `SA_RESTART` flag in `sa_flags`. If this flag is set, certain interrupted system calls will be automatically restarted by the kernel after the signal handler returns, instead of returning `EINTR`. However, not all system calls are restartable even with `SA_RESTART` (e.g., `select`, `poll`, `epoll_wait` are generally not restarted). It's often safer and more portable to explicitly check for `EINTR` and restart the call manually.

