**Edge-triggered behavior**: Events are only raised when the state **changes** (e.g., from "no data" to "data available"), not continuously while the condition is true.

## 2. Using socketpair() Instead of pipe()

**Yes, `socketpair()` can help!** It creates a bidirectional socket pair and often has better behavior with epoll:

````cpp
bool CgiHandler::setup_cgi_pipes(Connection* conn, int server_to_cgi_pipe[2],
                                 int cgi_to_server_pipe[2]) {
    // Use socketpair instead of pipe for better epoll behavior
    if (socketpair(AF_UNIX, SOCK_STREAM, 0, server_to_cgi_pipe) == -1) {
        log(LOG_ERROR, "socketpair server_to_cgi creation error: %s",
            strerror(errno));
        ErrorHandler::generate_error_response(conn, codes::INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR);
        return false;
    }

    if (socketpair(AF_UNIX, SOCK_STREAM, 0, cgi_to_server_pipe) == -1) {
        log(LOG_ERROR, "socketpair cgi_to_server creation error: %s",
            strerror(errno));
        close(server_to_cgi_pipe[0]);
        close(server_to_cgi_pipe[1]);
        ErrorHandler::generate_error_response(conn, codes::INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR);
        return false;
    }

    log(LOG_DEBUG, "CGI socketpairs created: server_to_cgi: %d,%d cgi_to_server: %d,%d",
        server_to_cgi_pipe[0], server_to_cgi_pipe[1], 
        cgi_to_server_pipe[0], cgi_to_server_pipe[1]);
