### Why This Approach is Superior

| Metric | Duplicating States | Using a Return State |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Code Reusability** | Poor. Logic for percent-encoding is copied. | **Excellent.** Logic is written once and reused. |
| **Scalability** | Poor. Adding a new URI component (e.g., fragment) requires another set of states. | **Excellent.** New components can reuse the same percent-encoding states. |
| **Maintainability** | Poor. A bug fix needs to be applied in multiple places. | **Excellent.** A bug fix is applied in one place. |
| **State Count** | High. Leads to a combinatorial explosion of states. | **Low.** Keeps the state machine lean and manageable. |

