 function is a standalone utility that takes a `std::string`. It has no guarantee that its input came from your validated parser.

An attacker could craft a request that bypasses other logic or exploits a different part of your server to call this function with a malformed string like `"/path/to/file%"`. This would cause your server to read past the end of the string, leading to a crash (Denial of Service) or potentially an information leak.

**The Fix:**
A robust utility function must always validate its own inputs. You must add a bounds check.

````cpp
