2.  **Future-Proofing (The Most Important Reason):** This is the key. Imagine in the future, a developer adds a primitive type or a raw pointer to your struct:
    ````cpp
    // filepath: /home/peters/Projects/webserv/include/HttpRequest.hpp
    // ...existing code...
    struct HttpRequest {
        // ...
        std::vector<char> body_;
        int               status_code_; // NEW: A primitive type
        Location*         location_;    // NEW: A raw pointer
        // ...
    };
